Fourteen hexagons through each edge
==================================

This component recovers only the existing F012 Table2 lower bound n(4,6,14)>=36. Read fourteen.pdf for the complete proof. The new boundary has seven exterior vertices inducing exactly one edge; its endpoints force equal side profiles.

Fresh verification::

  python check.py --study STUDY_ROOT --out NEW_DIRECTORY --render

The default repeats both complete target traversals (about eight minutes on the author machine). The explicit --reuse-recorded-targets mode instead verifies every byte of their complete retained execution closure; all finite controls, three sanitizer runs, independent oracles, damage controls and native build remain fresh. The author wrapper used this mode after the two full target runs had passed; this is disclosed, not called a fresh target rerun.

The initial completion reached its deadline and supplies no coverage. The changed necessary equal-profile restriction is in a separate file; initial bytes and receipts are retained. Primary and acquired results remain attributed. No whole-source, conjecture, priority, Lean or compression credit is assigned here.
